<!-- The yam v1 arm with the linear_4310 gripper and its RealSense D405 camera, as one
     self-contained model: joint1..joint6, the gripper body, the joint7/joint8 fingers, and the
     RealSense D405 camera as its own chain of bodies ending in the `camera` optical frame
     (+Z along the optical axis, ROS/OpenCV convention). It does NOT need combining with a
     gripper XML.

     Generated from yam_linear_4310_d405.urdf, the source of truth: every body, inertial and visual geom here
     places its mesh within 0.000 mm of that URDF. `tcp_site`/`grasp_site` and the joint7/joint8
     equality and contact exclusions come from gripper/linear_4310/linear_4310.xml.

     flange -> camera, i.e. `gripper` -> `camera`, is pos [-0.07, 0, -0.077], quat_wxyz
     [0.153, 0.69, 0.69, 0.153], the optical axis canted 25 deg off the flange -Z. That is the
     extrinsic tabulated in station/yam_station_linear_4310_d405/README.md, which is authoritative for
     it; the bodies below carry the same transform at full precision.

     joint7/joint8 follow the linear_4310 convention: q=0 is closed, positive opens -- the pad gap at
     `grasp_site` is 0.06 mm at q=0 and 93.96 mm at q=0.04695. The URDF drives them with the opposite
     sign; re-signing moves no geometry. -->
